172	    /**
173	     * The owner's identity key: the single derived value used to detect duplicate owners. It is the
174	     * normalized telephone, the (lower-cased) email or an empty string when absent, and the
175	     * household id or an empty string when absent, joined with {@code '|'} (e.g.
176	     * {@code "+61412345678|jo@example.com|3F2A9C1D4B6E8071"}). Two owners are the same person only
177	     * when their whole identity keys are equal; because the telephone is part of the key, household
178	     * members with different telephones have different keys.
179	     */
180	    public String getIdentityKey() {
181	        return String.join("|",
